(1039224, 123094, 11895, '<td valign="top">Congrats to Sammie on her first ribbon and the first ribbon for the FZ20.  A most deserving shot by a truely talented photographer. WTG!</td>', 'Congrats to Sammie on her first ribbon and the first ribbon for the FZ20.  A most deserving shot by a truely talented photographer. WTG!', '2004-11-30 21:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1039457, 123078, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kdolso:</b></div><hr/><i> This photo certainly give the illusion of movement. There is a hectic, frenetic tension. The artist captures the feeling of pushing the edge for me. The title doesn''t fit with my interpretation, but that is the beauty of subjective art. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks! Your comment pretty much expresses what I liked about this myself. It was a somewhat happy accident that the lights seem to form a stampeding herd of cars, and I did think later that "Stampede" might have been a better title ...<br/> <br/>The feeling and style this evoked for me -- and I hoped to pass on --  is related to the <a href="//www.turcantabria.com/Datos/Historia-Arte/Cuevas/Cuevas%20Altamira/altamira-fotos-i.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">paleolithic cave paintings</a> found mainly in Southern Europe, like those at <a href="//www.vm.kemsu.ru/en/palaeolith/altamira.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Altamira</a> in Spain and <a href="//www.vm.kemsu.ru/en/palaeolith/lascaux.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lascaux</a> in France -- a few simple strokes with some earth-based pigments and you suddenly have a thundering herd of antelope, horses, or bison. That was my first impression when I saw it pop up on the monitor when I got home.</td>', 'Originally posted by kdolso: This photo certainly give the illusion of movement. There is a hectic, frenetic tension. The artist captures the feeling of pushing the edge for me. The title doesn''t fit with my interpretation, but that is the beauty of subjective art.  Thanks! Your comment pretty much expresses what I liked about this myself. It was a somewhat happy accident that the lights seem to form a stampeding herd of cars, and I did think later that "Stampede" might have been a better title ... The feeling and style this evoked for me -- and I hoped to pass on --  is related to the paleolithic cave paintings found mainly in Southern Europe, like those at Altamira in Spain and Lascaux in France -- a few simple strokes with some earth-based pigments and you suddenly have a thundering herd of antelope, horses, or bison. That was my first impression when I saw it pop up on the monitor when I got home.', '2004-12-01 00:21:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1040118, 123165, 19959, '<td valign="top">Time Passing was a challenge that I suggested to DPChallenge. Your picture perfeclty reflects what I wanted the challenge to convey. A lot of entries to this challenge depicted ''passing time'' which is completely different.</td>', 'Time Passing was a challenge that I suggested to DPChallenge. Your picture perfeclty reflects what I wanted the challenge to convey. A lot of entries to this challenge depicted ''passing time'' which is completely different.', '2004-12-01 03:34:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1040590, 122354, 25500, '<td valign="top">A poem to accompany the photo:<br/> <br/>Where once there was laughter, rain erodes rock -<br/>surrogate tears for nearby mother''s grief<br/>buried heart and breast decaying or decayed<br/>shudders of woe long cease.<br/> <br/>Yet in this row, silenced children cue<br/>ribcages once possessing blood and gush and laugh and sigh<br/>no own stale air, dust, vacancy.<br/> <br/>Time, that slathering beast, that pilferer,<br/>that ravaging foe, that unbiased judge,<br/>takes all - less perhaps faith.</td>', 'A poem to accompany the photo: Where once there was laughter, rain erodes rock -surrogate tears for nearby mother''s griefburied heart and breast decaying or decayedshudders of woe long cease. Yet in this row, silenced children cueribcages once possessing blood and gush and laugh and sighno own stale air, dust, vacancy. Time, that slathering beast, that pilferer,that ravaging foe, that unbiased judge,takes all - less perhaps faith.', '2004-12-01 09:21:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1042218, 123168, 9668, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tyt2000:</b></div><hr/><i> Yeah this should have placed higher :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Ditto, Great shot sher!</td>', 'Originally posted by tyt2000: Yeah this should have placed higher :)  Ditto, Great shot sher!', '2004-12-01 20:58:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1043197, 123094, 24613, '<td valign="top">Congrats Sammie!!  Great shot!  You should have won a ribbon a long time ago with all your wonderful work!! :)</td>', 'Congrats Sammie!!  Great shot!  You should have won a ribbon a long time ago with all your wonderful work!! :)', '2004-12-02 11:53:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1043575, 122466, 20236, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SDW65:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice silhouette but a bit out of focus. This could have been a good photo it focus would have been on. I dont know if you used a tripod or not but my guess is camera shake. Keep up the good work, this one was very close. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry mate, the original file is in focus it blurred out when i made the 150k file for the challenge. Thanks anyway.</td>', 'Originally posted by SDW65: Nice silhouette but a bit out of focus. This could have been a good photo it focus would have been on. I dont know if you used a tripod or not but my guess is camera shake. Keep up the good work, this one was very close.   Sorry mate, the original file is in focus it blurred out when i made the 150k file for the challenge. Thanks anyway.', '2004-12-02 15:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1043629, 123038, 11793, '<td valign="top">fours seconds, and she didn''t move?  model?<br/>anyhow well done image.</td>', 'fours seconds, and she didn''t move?  model?anyhow well done image.', '2004-12-02 16:20:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1043967, 122466, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/> <br/>A very warm and soothing image. A little earlier would have allowed more cold colors, but the image as it stands is a wonderful study of the orange red spectrum. Of course, a sunrise or sunsets needs the touch of the silhoutte and here is where many images fail to entice. In this case the shrubs are ideal because they present a single subject to compare against the lovely sky colors. When this foreground is too busy, the viewer is intent in identifying shapes.<br/> <br/>Compositional wise it has the sun rising on the left and the shrubs framming it with a sweeping coolness across the the bottom and it is from this safe and comfortable darkness that we observe the sun.<br/> <br/>You have addressed the problem in the conversion and this is something you need to solve because if you enter an image and then you notice the deteriotion of the image, go do whatever to fix it, otherwise it is best to withdraw it because voters will simply mark it down.<br/> <br/>To conclude, your composition is above average and by maintaining this quality you will turn in some very attractive images.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-02 20:36:54.</i></td>', 'from the critique club: A very warm and soothing image. A little earlier would have allowed more cold colors, but the image as it stands is a wonderful study of the orange red spectrum. Of course, a sunrise or sunsets needs the touch of the silhoutte and here is where many images fail to entice. In this case the shrubs are ideal because they present a single subject to compare against the lovely sky colors. When this foreground is too busy, the viewer is intent in identifying shapes. Compositional wise it has the sun rising on the left and the shrubs framming it with a sweeping coolness across the the bottom and it is from this safe and comfortable darkness that we observe the sun. You have addressed the problem in the conversion and this is something you need to solve because if you enter an image and then you notice the deteriotion of the image, go do whatever to fix it, otherwise it is best to withdraw it because voters will simply mark it down. To conclude, your composition is above average and by maintaining this quality you will turn in some very attractive images.', '2004-12-02 20:35:01.000000', '2004-12-02 20:36:54.000000', 0),
(1044156, 123054, 17203, '<td valign="top">Wow! Amazing placement considering how brief this period of time is. Congrats! You really do a great job with backgrounds and lighting- added you to my favorites. ;-)</td>', 'Wow! Amazing placement considering how brief this period of time is. Congrats! You really do a great job with backgrounds and lighting- added you to my favorites. ;-)', '2004-12-02 23:36:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1044283, 121590, 9581, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot! Awesome composition with the best light!</td>', 'Very nice shot! Awesome composition with the best light!', '2004-12-03 01:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1045243, 121590, 22479, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your feedback, much appreciated!</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your feedback, much appreciated!', '2004-12-03 20:45:12.000000', NULL, 0),
